# pii-guard allowlist — intentional, reviewed matches that are OK to ship.
#
# ERE patterns matched against "file:line:content" hit lines; any match is
# excluded from the scan. This file IS tracked (it only describes what's
# allowed, never the sensitive list itself). Keep it tiny and justify each line.
#
# The LICENSE file is intentionally public boilerplate + the maintainer's name
# in the copyright line; allow the whole file. The contact email in the README
# is also meant to be public.
^LICENSE:
^README\.md:.*@

# The Go module path / GitHub handle is the project's intended public identity
# (import paths, go.mod, clone URL, ghcr image, CI badge, macOS bundle id).
# This narrowly excludes the squashed handle only — "Jason Dostal" with a space
# still flags via the surname pattern.
jasondostal
com\.jasondostal

# The "Cairn" color preset is an intentional, kept homage — it's only a theme
# name, meaningless to outsiders. Matches the preset definition in theme.js and
# Theme.swift; bare "Cairn" anywhere else still flags.
name: ['"]Cairn['"]
